{
 "_about": "Labeled benchmark for evaluating AgrAgent tool-selection behavior, v2 (126 queries). 'groups' is a list of intent groups; the agent must call at least one tool from EACH group (interchangeable alternatives within a group). 'gold' is the flat set of acceptable tools (no false-positive penalty). Empty groups + gold = out-of-scope (agent should abstain from tool use). Ground-truth labels assigned by the authors. v2 extends v1 (63 queries, unchanged and carried through verbatim as Q01-Q63) with 63 further queries. Two extensions are substantive: out-of-scope items now include requests that are plausibly agronomic but unsupported by the platform ('unsupported_request' subtype), which is a harder abstention test than the greetings and general-knowledge items of v1; and three compound queries require three intent groups, where v1 never exceeded two. Open-source release (v2.0.0): derived from v2 by removing 'search_inia_rag', which is not part of the public agent (its corpus is not redistributable); in every group where it appeared, 'search_inia_biblioteca' remains as the INIA alternative, so no query lost a group. Queries changed: Q22, Q23, Q24, Q25, Q26, Q27, Q36, Q37, Q45, Q56, Q101, Q102, Q103, Q104, Q105, Q106, Q107, Q108, Q114, Q115, Q118. The public agent also exposes 'geocode_place', an auxiliary lookup that is not a labelled intent: the harness ignores it when scoring in-scope queries and counts it as a tool call for out-of-scope abstention.",
 "_source": "agent_benchmark_v2.json (126 queries), unchanged except as described in _about",
